- venue: Nature Communications
- citation count: 194
[method]
The paper used a combined anatomical and ultrastructural approach to map DR VGluT3 axonal contacts onto TH-positive dendrites in mesoaccumbens and VTA. As indicated by the section headings, the method involved fluorescence microscopy with three-dimensional analysis to identify and reconstruct DR VGluT3 axons and their apposition to TH-positive dendrites, followed by electron microscopy and ultrastructural analysis to confirm synaptic organization. Functional readouts were tied to DR-VGluT3 afferent activation, including mesoaccumbens TH neuronal activation, instrumental responding after VTA VGluT3-afferent activation, and AMPA-mediated place preference in VTA. This is related to the proposed method because it addresses whether dorsal raphe projections form excitatory synaptic inputs onto TH-positive neurons in NAc/VTA, a circuit relevant to the plan's goal of mapping DRN SERT neuron inputs in DS, NAc shell, OFC, and VTA; however, the paper method is not the proposed optogenetic whole-cell EPSC assay.
[results]
The available headings report that most DR-VGluT3 axons synapse on TH-positive dendrites; that DR VGluT3 neurons synapse on mesoaccumbens TH neurons; that DR-VGluT3 afferent activation activated mesoaccumbens TH neurons; that VTA VGluT3-afferent activation supported instrumental responding; and that VTA AMPA-mediated place preference was observed. No numerical values, sample sizes, baseline comparisons, or statistical significance values are provided in the supplied text.
[context]
The supplied text does not specify viral constructs, animal numbers, imaging hardware, reconstruction software, electron microscopy parameters, stimulation parameters, slice conditions, or statistical tests. The context inferable from the headings is that DR VGluT3 neurons were labeled or identified, TH-positive dendrites were used as the target population, three-dimensional fluorescence analysis and electron microscopy were used to establish synaptic contacts, and statistical analysis was applied to the anatomical or functional comparisons. This context supports the proposed research plan by showing that DR glutamatergic projections can contact TH-positive neurons in mesoaccumbens and VTA, but it does not directly establish SERT-specific DRN synaptic inputs or optogenetically evoked EPSCs in DS, anterior/posterior NAc shell, OFC, or VTA.
[end related work 1]

