[results]
The reported outcomes were qualitative in the provided excerpt: morphine injection produced anatomically distinct dopamine increases in medial and lateral NAc, morphine altered spontaneous dopamine transient activity, and recurrent morphine treatment did not shift the dopamine response to IV morphine in the NAc shell. No numerical ΔF/F values, effect sizes, sample sizes, or statistical p-values are available in the supplied text.
