  "contradictions": "The strongest contradiction is also from [(Salinas et al., 2023-09)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/6d2080c01166b331aa2335fba07d7254f855731b), which showed that apparent DAT inhibitor effects on FSCV were method-dependent, changed when electrode adsorption was altered, and were absent in DAT knockout mice, indicating that cocaine-like DAT blockade can produce sensor or electrode signals that do not straightforwardly reflect a true increase in dopamine release. This directly challenges the proposal's assumption that passive cocaine injection can serve as a clean positive control for optogenetically evoked vesicular DA release and that peak or 5-second AUC after cocaine can be directly compared with optogenetic stimulation. A second contradiction is that cocaine is a reuptake blocker rather than a pure release stimulus, so it may generate a slower tonic DA elevation, whereas the proposed optogenetic protocol consists of short 4-ms laser pulses at 20 Hz in 5-pulse bursts separated by 250 ms and is intended to evoke phasic release; comparing these two time courses with peak and short AUC windows may conflate reuptake inhibition with vesicular release. A weaker contradiction comes from [(Bernklau et al., 2024-01)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/d697e2d867ff19078ec70a9ad91fca8745a25c8a), which showed that phasic DA signals depend on learned behavior, choice strategy, and prediction-error context, implying that DA dynamics in a passive open-field cocaine experiment may not be directly comparable to DA dynamics during optogenetic stimulation or to task-related phasic release. Finally, neither related work supports using cocaine as a positive control for the proposed 5-HT sensor GRAB5HT, because both studies are DA-focused and do not provide evidence that cocaine robustly elevates striatal 5-HT in the same way it elevates dLight signals.",
  "suggested_action": "The most important action is to reframe cocaine as a positive control for sensor responsiveness and DA-elevating/reuptake blockade, not as a direct measure of optogenetic vesicular release, and to add a separate 5-HT positive control for GRAB5HT, such as optogenetic DRN SERT stimulation, a 5-HT agonist, or a validated 5-HT release protocol, because cocaine is not supported by the related work as a 5-HT positive control. The next most important action is to add quantitative validation of the 15 mg/kg cocaine response, including vehicle controls, dose-response or at least pilot dose confirmation, and reporting of peak Delta F/F, latency, AUC, decay time, tonic versus phasic components, effect sizes, p-values, and sample sizes, using transient decay analysis as in [(Salinas et al., 2023-09)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/6d2080c01166b331aa2335fba07d7254f855731b) to separate slow cocaine-evoked tonic DA from faster optogenetic phasic DA. A third action is to include a subset of FSCV or DAT-knockout validation, or at minimum explicitly acknowledge the FSCV method-dependence shown by [(Salinas et al., 2023-09)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/6d2080c01166b331aa2335fba07d7254f855731b), to reduce the risk that cocaine or optogenetic signals are misinterpreted as release when they may reflect reuptake, sensor kinetics, or electrode artifacts. A fourth action is to control and report behavioral state, because [(Bernklau et al., 2024-01)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/d697e2d867ff19078ec70a9ad91fca8745a25c8a) shows DA phasic signals are behavior- and strategy-dependent; the plan should track movement, restrict or quantify open-field behavior, align optogenetic and cocaine epochs, and possibly include a simple behavioral task or movement-corrected analysis. A fifth action is to specify implementation details for reproducibility, including sensor expression levels, viral titers, fiber photometry wavelengths, LED intensities, sampling rate, motion correction, photobleating correction, histology, a pre-registered MATLAB analysis pipeline, and statistical model, and to use event-locked analysis for optogenetic pulses and cocaine injection as in [(Bernklau et al., 2024-01)](https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/d697e2d867ff19078ec70a9ad91fca8745a25c8a). A final action is to adjust the optogenetic comparison by testing single-pulse, paired-pulse, and longer stimulation conditions so that the DA and 5-HT time courses can be matched to the cocaine time course and to the kinetic differences between dLight1.2 and GRAB5HT.",
